hyperhermes: the hermes vault through the host's vault broker
(modules/core/vault-broker.nix), so the agent's own uid cannot read it.

hermes v0.23.0 keeps the vault in <HERMES_HOME>/vault/ (vault.json.enc
and its Fernet key vault.key beside it), owned by the agent's uid; every
terminal command and script the model runs could decrypt it.

Change (agent/vault_store.py): when root's marker
/run/hermes-vault/<user>.on exists (the directory root's and closed to
others, else the vault refuses to work), VaultStore's public API (add_item, list_items, has_items,
remove_item, get_meta, resolve_secret) goes to that broker for the home
the store's directory belongs to (<home>/vault: the agent's home or a
profile) over /run/hermes-vault/<user>.sock. One connection per request, close-on-exec, closed before
returning; a server running as the caller's own uid is refused (an
impostor); no fallback to the files. key_location reports "broker",
migrate_key refuses, own_copied_key is a no-op (the copied directory
holds no key). The broker's own store is VaultStore(direct=True).
hermes_cli/vault.py: `hermes vault key` says where the key is.
The fill path, consent and redaction are unchanged; the broker hands
values only to the agent's gateway or dashboard process.

